         Mission Statement At the heart of Orange’s local government, the Town Clerk’s Office is here to connect, inform, and serve. We strive to make every interaction welcoming, every process accessible, and every record reliable. We are dedicated to providing reliable information, preserving the town’s history, and supporting fair and transparent elections while working collaboratively to meet the evolving needs of our residents. With a commitment to promoting open government and public trust, and as the stewards of the town’s official records, elections, and vital services, we ensure accuracy, accessibility, and accountability in all that we do. We work collaboratively to empower residents, support transparency, and uphold the democratic process at the local level. Description of Services The Town Clerk’s Office serves as the central hub of information, records, and civic activity for the Town of Orange, providing essential services to residents, businesses, and visitors.  Responsibilities include: Administering all local, state, and federal elections, ensuring fair, secure, and accessible voting Serving as custodian of public records and recording official actions of Town Meeting Maintaining and issuing certified vital records, including births, deaths, and marriages Processing licenses and permits such as marriage licenses, business certificates, dog licenses, and other state and local permits Managing public records requests and ensuring compliance with Massachusetts laws Providing guidance, information, and support to the public, as well as to town boards, committees, and departments The Town Clerk's Office is where community, records, and service meet. 
     

 
